/-!
# H-free bridge, pieces 3 and 4 on the slice: `hdefer_holds`

At every normalized place `v` of `L0 = Frac(K[X,Y,Y',Γ]/(F₀))` over the slice (`ν ∘ ψ = v^e`),
`v` is trivial on `k = K(ℓ, X)`, `(ℓ, X)` is algebraically independent, and one of the two
free coordinates `x_a` (the slice form eliminates `x_i`) is transcendental over `k`: at a pole
of a free coordinate, that coordinate; at an affine place, `Y` or `Γ` (`q 1 = 0` or `i = 1`).
The other free coordinate satisfies the slice relation of degree `≤ N` (`core_poly`), and the
Dedekind `engine` gives `CrudeBound` and `ResiduallySeparable`.
-/

